    "result_text": "That exclusion is only for JaCoCo coverage (generated code), not test execution. Everything checks out.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `timezone` field derived from the owner's locality/region, following the existing derived-field pattern in the codebase:\n\n1. **`LocalityResolver.java`** \u2014 added the fixed region-to-timezone table (`NSW\u2192Australia/Sydney`, `VIC\u2192Australia/Melbourne`, `QLD\u2192Australia/Brisbane`) and a `timezoneFor(String region)` lookup method. This keeps region knowledge co-located with the class that already owns region/postcode/city resolution, and returns `null` for regions with no known timezone (e.g. `UNKNOWN`).\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `@Transient getTimezone()` derived getter that delegates to `LocalityResolver.timezoneFor(getLocality())`, mirroring how `getLocality()`, `getCheckDigit()`, and `getAgeBand()` are computed.\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `timezone` string property to the `OwnerDto` schema (next to `locality`), so the generated DTO gains the field and MapStruct maps it automatically from `Owner.getTimezone()` \u2014 no mapper changes needed.\n\nThe test suite passes: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 the acceptance test asserting `locality == \"NSW\"` and `timezone == \"Australia/Sydney\"` for a Sydney owner is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
